.\" Manual page for zirbe. @VERSION@ is filled in by build-deb.sh.
.\"
.\" Author: David M. Anderson
.\" Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
.TH ZIRBE 1 "2026\-11\-09" "zirbe @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zirbe \- email that reads like a conversation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zirbe
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Zirbe
shows the mail in an IMAP account as conversations. A conversation is an
email thread, joined by its Message\-ID, In\-Reply\-To and References headers;
its subject is the conversation's name, the people on From, To and Cc are its
members, and each message is a bubble. Mail you sent, read from the account's
Sent folder, sits on the right.
.PP
A reply goes to everyone in the conversation and carries the threading headers,
so it stays in the thread for every other mail program. A new conversation
needs a name, which becomes its subject.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Show sample conversations instead of the accounts signed in.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Send the reply being written; Shift+Enter starts a new line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Start a new conversation.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Check for mail now.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/zirbe/accounts.json
The accounts signed in: address, name and servers, with no password.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/zirbe/
The newest messages of each account's inbox and Sent folder, readable only by the user.
.PP
Passwords are kept in the desktop keyring under the attribute
.BR service=zirbe ,
with the account's address as
.BR username .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns success when the window has been closed. A non\-zero status means the
window could not be created at all: no display, or no usable graphics driver.
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
